From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:35:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Submit live shared frame transfers

Frame-server clients can provide a destination texture shared with a native
renderer through an NT handle and keyed mutex.  The render transfer queued its
draw and returned without submitting the D3D11 immediate context.  A consumer
outside that context could therefore observe the old texture contents even
though TransferVideoFrame returned success.

Flush live transfers to shared destination textures before returning control
to the external consumer.  Keep ordinary Media Engine playback and unshared
textures on the existing asynchronous path.
---
 dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -3348,6 +3348,10 @@ static HRESULT media_engine_transfer_to_d3d11_texture(struct media_engine *engin
 
     ID3D11DeviceContext_Draw(context, 4, 0);
 
+    if (isinf(engine->duration) && (desc.MiscFlags & (D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED_KEYEDMUTEX
+            | D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED_NTHANDLE)))
+        ID3D11DeviceContext_Flush(context);
+
     ID3D11RenderTargetView_Release(rtv);
     ID3D11DeviceContext_Release(context);
 
-- 
